Experiment: The Abuse Rig – Exception Handling and Program Testing
Course: CS-1281 | Python Programming Lab
Department: Production Engineering, VSSUT Burla
Date: 11-09-2026

1. Aim
To understand Python exception handling and improve program reliability by testing parsers and machine classes with invalid inputs.

2. Objectives
IT12: Create eight test cases using invalid and unexpected inputs.
IT10: Harden the log parser using named exceptions and a rejects list.
IT8: Protect the machine class using custom exceptions.
IT6: Develop an automated testing function using run_tests().
3. Concepts Used
Exception handling (try, except)
ValueError, TypeError, IndexError, KeyError
Custom exceptions
raise statement
Input validation
Rejects list and error reporting
Automated testing and pass/fail results
4. Testing and Certification
The program is tested against eight hostile inputs, including:

Blank input and empty records.
Missing fields.
Incorrect numerical values.
Invalid data types.
Unexpected and out-of-range readings.
Missing dictionary keys.
Invalid machine operating commands.
Zero or invalid values during calculations.
5. Error Handling
Use named exceptions instead of bare except.
Store rejected records with their error reasons.
Prevent invalid readings from affecting averages.
Use custom exceptions such as SpecViolation.
Ensure one faulty job does not stop the entire fleet.
6. Certification Criteria
All eight tests must pass.
No bare except statements.
Valid data must produce the same output as before.
Rejects table must display faulty records and reasons.
Final result must show PASS or FAIL for each test.
7. Result
Successfully studied exception handling, input validation, custom exceptions and automated testing to improve Python program reliability.

8. Conclusion
Exception handling makes industrial programs safer and more reliable by identifying errors, rejecting invalid data and preventing unexpected program termination.
